{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1024995-time-effect-to-increase-your-initiative","id":1024995,"title":"Time Effect to Increase Your Initiative","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-31T21:11:37-08:00","id":1024995,"title":"Time Effect to Increase Your Initiative","content":"So what do you think would be required? Is this a Time 3 effect only with each success moving you up one spot on the initiative ladder? Or could 3 successes on a Time 3 effect just make you go first? If not how bout 5?<br /> <br /> Or do you think Time 1 or 2 could pull this off? I do lean toward needing Time 3 though with a Time 1 effect maybe giving a +1 to the Initiative Roll.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T04:52:48-08:00","id":1025052,"title":"","content":"Time 1 can percieve how much time /exactly/ would someone (or something) take to accomplish certain goal, and in our case, that's combat which probably means hitting you or somebody else (or defending, etc). Knowing that precise momentum might already help, and if not--<br /> <br /> You can always refer to Time 2, which is predicting future. Knowing when they will strike gives you an upper hand in mental part of initiative (relating to Wits, which directly contribute to initiative rating).<br /> <br /> But, at the end of a day, Time 3 is capable of accelerating. Usually it's used for extra actions and whatnot, but I guess you could do it to accelerate physically (relating to Dexterity, which directly contributes to initiative rating as well). Though, why go for physical juju and get higher difficulty if Time 2 should certainly do the job?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T05:45:46-08:00","id":1025057,"title":"","content":"The way I usually do combat is I allow any player the choice to delay their actions for an entire round in order to get to the top of the initiative order next round. I multiple people do this then those people go to the top of the round in their current order, so if everyone delays, nothing happens.<br /> Perhaps if someone has a Time 1 effect active, they would always remain at the top of the initiative even if other players delay.<br /> <br /> You could argue that Time 1 would help you cordinate your moves with greater precision, allowing you to change proclaimed actions without needing a willpower roll, or to react to someone's attack with less fumbling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T06:05:16-08:00","id":1025059,"title":"","content":"An effect that was used by my group with Mage and Ed was Corr 1 / Mind 2 / Time 1 to guage the intended actions of others by reading their surface thoughts and figuring time and location required of those intentions. The game effect was everyone opposed got a Willpower (TN: 8) to oppose the successes. Those that failed had their initiative result changed to be worse than the caster (in the same order if multiple failed). And if the opponent(s) changed their actions, the caster knew it before they resolved by a split second. Didn't work on timed events without a mind guiding them, like a ticking bomb or oncoming train.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T11:34:50-08:00","id":1025124,"title":"","content":"Well it takes a whole turn to use Arete, so it's kind of self-defeating unless you enact it before combat. I'd probably give a +2 bonus to initiative per Time 3 success if they wanted to keep it Coincidental; if they wanted 1 success to guarantee they go first, it would be Vulgar. Or something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:55:29-08:00","id":1026045,"title":"","content":"Seems easier to just boost Wits and Dex directly with Mind/Life.<br /> <br /> I'd probably allow someone to use that Time Loop power to go first in initiative if they had the thing that let them remember what happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:07:25-08:00","id":1026054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1024995-time-effect-to-increase-your-initiative?p=1026045#post1026045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems easier to just boost Wits and Dex directly with Mind/Life.<br /> <br /> I'd probably allow someone to use that Time Loop power to go first in initiative if they had the thing that let them remember what happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time 3 on its own should be enough. You only need the &quot;remember what happened&quot; stuff if you're trying to Time loop your body to, for example, remove damage but not your mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}